import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About — The Gentle AI Guide"
  description="Who is behind The Gentle AI Guide, why it exists, and how every guide is written and reviewed."
>
  <section class="section section--hero">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>About this site</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Gentle AI Guide exists for one reason: the people who could benefit most
        from AI are the ones nobody is explaining it to.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
  <p>
    Most writing about AI is aimed at experts, investors, or people who already
    use it every day. If you're not one of them, it can feel like the world
    changed while nobody showed you where the door is. This site is that door —
    calm, unhurried, and in plain English.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
  <p>
    The Gentle AI Guide is made by <strong>Jacob S. Olsen</strong>, an
    independent website publisher in Denmark. You can reach him any time at
    <a href="mailto:hello@gentleaiguide.com">hello@gentleaiguide.com</a> —
    questions from readers often become new guides.
  </p>

  <h2>How the guides are written</h2>
  <p>
    Honesty first: the guides on this site are written with the help of AI —
    the same kind of tool the site teaches you to use. Every guide is then read,
    corrected and approved by a person before it is published, and each page
    shows the date it was last reviewed.
  </p>
  <p>
    We work this way on purpose. It's exactly the relationship with AI we
    recommend to you in the guides: let it do the heavy lifting, but never let
    it have the final word.
  </p>

  <h2>What we promise</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Plain English.</strong> Every technical word is explained the first time it appears.</li>
    <li><strong>No hype, no fear.</strong> We tell you what AI is genuinely good at and where it fails.</li>
    <li><strong>No pressure.</strong> Nothing here to buy, no account to create, nothing to install.</li>
    <li><strong>Your pace.</strong> Guides are written to be read slowly, and re-read.</li>
  </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
